      summary: "Himachal Pradesh grew out of a mosaic of ancient western-Himalayan chiefdoms and Rajput hill states such as Kangra, Chamba, Mandi and Sirmaur. The hills passed under Mughal, Sikh and finally British paramountcy in the 19th century. On 15 April 1948 some 30 princely hill states were merged into a new Chief Commissioner's Province, which became a union territory in 1956 and India's 18th state on 25 January 1971.",
