        medieval: "Through the medieval centuries the region was divided among long-lived Rajput hill states — Kangra under its Katoch rulers, together with Chamba, Kullu, Mandi, Bushahr and Sirmaur — which paid tribute at various times to the sultans of Delhi and the Mughals while keeping local autonomy in their mountain fastnesses. Kangra fort was the most contested prize of the hills, drawing repeated invasions from the plains.",
